Let me think about the most idiomatic way:

```rust
pub fn filter_by_tag<'a>(notes: &'a [Note], tag: &str) -> Vec<&'a Note> {
    notes
        .iter()
        .filter(|note| note.tags.iter().any(|t| t == tag))
        .cloned()
        .collect()
}
```

This uses `Iterator::filter` and `Iterator::cloned` to create a vector of references
. This preserves the order and is efficient.

